      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Mitchell Berman was raised in a one-stoplight town in rural Wisconsin where neighbors looked out for one another and values like community, honesty, and integrity weren't just taught – they were lived. His father built a small roofing business from the ground up and his mother worked long hours grinding pistons at the local foundry. Growing up, Mitchell spent his days hunting, fishing and going to church. His parents taught him to work hard, lend a hand, and root for the Packers. A proud product of Wisconsin's public schools, Mitchell was the first in his family to graduate from college – earning his degree while working three jobs, living paycheck to paycheck, and taking out student loans.",
